msgstr "Z row · piano keys"

msgid "KEYBOARD_HOME"
msgstr "A row · piano keys"

msgid "KEYBOARD_OCTAVE"
msgstr "Starting C octave"

msgid "KEYBOARD_EXPLAIN"
msgstr "An octave repeats the same note names higher or lower. Keyboard notes use the instrument volume and appear as diamonds on the staff, with outlined frets at the playhead. A ! means no free guitar string can play that note. Notes are not recorded or scored. See Help for the keys."

msgid "KEYBOARD_HELP_LOWER"
msgstr "Keyboard: Z X C V B N M , play C D E F G A B C. S D G H J play the black piano keys (sharps/flats). − and = lower/raise the octave. Hold a key to sustain; release to stop. Notes work in practice, including while paused, and are disabled in menus."

msgid "KEYBOARD_HELP_HOME"
msgstr "Keyboard: A S D F G H J K play C D E F G A B C. W E T Y U play the black piano keys (sharps/flats). Z/X or −/= lower/raise the octave. Hold a key to sustain; release to stop. Notes work in practice, including while paused, and are disabled in menus."

